# Auto-Memory Soft Delete

File-backed auto-memory deletes must be soft deletes:

- Remove the active pointer from `MEMORY.md`.
- Move the memory file under `.trash/` inside the same memory root.
- Add tombstone metadata: `deleted`, `deleted_at`, `delete_reason`,
  and `original_path`.
- Treat repeated deletes as idempotent success when the active file is already gone.
- Hard delete only through a retention-aware garbage collector scoped to `.trash/`.

Do not use shell `rm`, broad filesystem unlink, or edit-only tombstones that
leave active index references.

When the memory root is mounted, use:

```bash
scripts/memory_soft_delete.py delete \
  --root <memory-root> \
  --path <relative-memory.md> \
  --reason <reason>
```
